From 1e84dfeefb9b69b3cf385f9635d05d7937ddcb60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias <ruck.tobias@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Apr 2021 09:36:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Enforce Logos coinbase rule on testnet (#143)

Testnet coins are worthless anyway; this will allow mining pools to test their setup.
It'll also allow us to test new coinbase outputs on the testnet.

Rebase provenance: this historical change was adapted onto the pinned
Bitcoin ABC base. Source diff is the recorded Lotus V1 replay commit below.

Historical-source-commit: 1852483756bf9faeb24133b2bfb107602bf35cda
Recorded-replay-commit: 98212cdb269670ba4ea10f457bee29ec21bbbd99

diff --git a/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp b/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
index c21ca42aaf..45f8c6f75a 100644
--- a/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
+++ b/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
@@ -260,8 +260,8 @@ public:
         // two days
         consensus.nDAAHalfLife = 2 * 24 * 60 * 60;
 
-        // The miner fund is disabled by default on testnet.
-        consensus.enableMinerFund = false;
+        // The miner fund is enabled by default on testnet.
+        consensus.enableMinerFund = true;
 
         // The staking rewards are disabled by default on testnet.
         consensus.enableStakingRewards = false;
